{
  "schema_version": "1.7.0",
  "id": "USN-9050-1",
  "summary": "davical vulnerabilities",
  "details": "It was discovered that DAViCal did not properly encode certain request\nparameters, leading to a reflected cross-site scripting vulnerability. A\nremote attacker could possibly use this issue to perform actions as another\nuser, including adding administrator accounts. (CVE-2019-18345)\n\nIt was discovered that DAViCal did not protect against cross-site request\nforgery. A remote attacker could possibly use this issue to perform actions\nas an authenticated user, including adding administrator accounts.\n(CVE-2019-18346)\n\nIt was discovered that DAViCal did not properly sanitize certain user\naccount fields, leading to a stored cross-site scripting vulnerability. An\nauthenticated user could possibly use this issue to execute arbitrary\nscript in the browser of another user, including an administrator.\n(CVE-2019-18347)",
